A||N||9||Steve Normington||Isuzu 5-spd & V-6||||1||
Z||000000||Steve Normington||04-08-2001||12:58 PM||||Does anyone have experience using the Isuzu 5-spd with the V-6? I know GM didn't think it would work, but what do they know? I'm thinking of hooking a 3.1 to the 5-spd since it is supposed to be the best gear ratio, but I don't want to be busting the tranny on a regular basis. If you have done this, what kind of reliability have you had and did you have to do any mods to the transmission?<P>------------------<BR>85 SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||04-08-2001||01:22 PM||||Please see the thread called Northstar standard shift. It will have your answer.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||04-08-2001||03:10 PM||||In short, yes.  I think when my Getrag goes I will just throw in an Isuzu.  Getrags cost about $700-$1,000 dollars in comparison to Isuzu's which you can find for $100-$200.  So even if you break 4 Isuzu's your just about equal with the price of 1 Getrag!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">  <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||04-08-2001||10:03 PM||||From what I've heard, the weakest part of the Isuzu is the shift fork(s). I just wouldn't recommend speed-shifting. <BR>Several folks on the forum have Isuzus behind V-6s. Even 3.4s. I have even seen one V-8 through an Isuzu. Have never heard of one breaking. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000004||87ECO5||04-09-2001||08:51 AM||||I have an Isuzu bolted to my 3.6.  The tranny has some grinding problems (I believe due to bad synchros) but it seems to do OK otherwise.  Like Raydar said, I've heard it's not recommended to shift very quickly.<P>I've only had this combination for about 600 miles now so I'm obviously not the best person to ask about long-term durability.<P>On a happy note, Ed Parks (the guy that did my conversion) said that the 3.6/Isuzu combo is good for a top speed of 150 miles per hour!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   Not that my Fiero will ever see that with ME piloting it!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000005||Carrolles||04-09-2001||09:51 AM||||Is a 3.6 a bored out 3.4?||||reg||1
Z||000006||rockcrawl||04-09-2001||06:58 PM||||A lot of people prefer the ratios and smoothness of an Isuzu. I personally have had one with a broken shift fork. That has nothing to do with power handling capability, it was on a 2.5. Easy to fix, cheaper to get a new one. Denise of Del-Val Fieros has one on her 2.8 for at least a year with no problem. Archie says they work fine with a V8, I believe him. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||87ECO5||04-10-2001||08:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Carrolles:<BR><B>Is a 3.6 a bored out 3.4?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep.||||reg||14
Z||000008||WKDFIRO||04-10-2001||08:32 PM||||A long time ago we built up a 3.2 V6 to replace a 2.5 and used the Isuzu. While we were putting it into the car we too were wondering about if the tranny could really take it. The customer was a nutty cowboy in every sense of the word. While visiting he was telling us about how the only way to find out if something works is to break it. We stopped and looked at each other and very much expected this tranny to come back and haunt us. We know this guy beat it up. He doesn't know how to do anything BUT speed shift. He speed shifts in a parking lot!<P>Never heard a peep out of that Isuzu 5 speed tranny...||||reg||4
Z||000009||TheFiero64||04-11-2001||04:14 PM||||I love my Isuzu 5. I have it in my 88 with the 2.8. I am not light on it either. I've driven it hard and it shifts like new. The trans. has 170,000 on it too. There is also someone in my Fiero club that has this setup and she loves it.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
